1
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,160
A cripple?

2
00:02:12,850 --> 00:02:14,470
You let a cripple escape?

3
00:02:15,810 --> 00:02:17,390
The boy can't walk,

4
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:19,210
but somehow he slipped past you?

5
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,730
The giant must have took him.

6
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:26,020
The giant?

7
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:27,900
Hodor?

8
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:31,350
Oh, well, that's all right, then.

9
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:34,040
You let a halfwit escape with a cripple.

10
00:02:35,210 --> 00:02:37,050
And Rickon, too? The little one?

11
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:39,920
Gone, along with the wildling woman,

12
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:42,460
the one you were fucking.

13
00:03:02,170 --> 00:03:06,240
Right, get the horses and the hounds.

14
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,390
Come on, find the scent.

15
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:17,090
Come on, where they going?

16
00:03:27,630 --> 00:03:28,720
Halt!

17
00:03:33,430 --> 00:03:34,760
Enjoying your first hunt?

18
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:38,020
So far, hunting seems very similar to riding, My Lord.

19
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:41,210
- With hunting, there's blood at the end. - They're little boys.

20
00:03:41,210 --> 00:03:44,640
I was a little boy when I was torn away from my home and brought here.

21
00:03:45,020 --> 00:03:46,480
So I kept my word.

22
00:03:46,610 --> 00:03:47,960
I never ran away.

23
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:51,660
If I find them soon enough, I won't hurt them.

24
00:03:53,150 --> 00:03:55,770
Well, I'll hurt them, but I won't kill them.

25
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:59,140
Those boys are of far more value to you alive than dead.

26
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:00,750
They have no value to me missing.

27
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:03,220
Robb will have sent a force to retake Winterfell by now.

28
00:04:03,230 --> 00:04:06,480
Robb's in the riverlands. My sister's in Deepwood Motte.

29
00:04:06,490 --> 00:04:08,880
She'll get here long before they do.

30
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:11,120
And Ned Stark always said

31
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:14,250
500 men could hold Winterfell against 10,000.

32
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:16,400
We have a scent!

33
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:18,050
The hounds have the scent.

34
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:22,140
Come, Maester, don't look so grim.

35
00:04:22,750 --> 00:04:24,080
It's all just a game.

36
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:41,990
We should have took more food.

37
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:43,810
We couldn't risk going to the kitchens.

38
00:04:43,810 --> 00:04:45,310
Those people all love you.

39
00:04:45,310 --> 00:04:46,710
They would have given you whatever you needed.

40
00:04:46,710 --> 00:04:48,780
And if Theon found out, he'd hang them.

41
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:51,880
- The boy can't survive on walnuts. - I'm fine.

42
00:04:53,430 --> 00:04:55,890
We've been walking since before sunrise.

43
00:04:55,950 --> 00:04:58,440
- Even Hodor will tire. - Hodor.

44
00:04:58,480 --> 00:05:01,110
- Even you, sweet giant. - Hodor.

45
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:07,380
Wait, I know that farm.

46
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:09,710
I sent those two Winterfell orphans there.

47
00:05:10,690 --> 00:05:11,940
Jack and Billy.

48
00:05:12,190 --> 00:05:13,250
They'll give us some food.

49
00:05:13,250 --> 00:05:14,650
We can't risk it.

50
00:05:14,650 --> 00:05:16,750
If Theon tracks us here, he'll torture them

51
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,430
until he finds out where we are.

52
00:05:18,590 --> 00:05:20,950
Billy climbs a tree better than anyone.

53
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:23,130
You've never seen me climb a tree, little man.

54
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:25,330
They'll be after us with hounds.

55
00:05:25,550 --> 00:05:27,090
We got a good start on them,

56
00:05:27,090 --> 00:05:29,270
but we can't outrun hounds forever.

57
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:57,130
Did you pull a knife on me in the night?

58
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:09,070
What's the matter?

59
00:06:09,510 --> 00:06:12,640
Can't be the first time you pressed your bone against a woman's ass.

60
00:06:14,970 --> 00:06:16,140
Let's move.

61
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:24,820
Oh, it is the first time.

62
00:06:26,090 --> 00:06:27,830
How old are you, boy?

63
00:06:28,530 --> 00:06:30,670
I'm a man of the Night's Watch.

64
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:35,650
You're a boy who's never been with a girl.

65
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:40,880
Don't your stones start to hurt

66
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:42,640
if your bone never gets--

67
00:06:43,810 --> 00:06:45,130
Don't call them that.

68
00:06:45,690 --> 00:06:47,060
What, stones?

69
00:06:49,110 --> 00:06:50,380
Or bone?

70
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:52,050
Neither.

71
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:54,500
Both.

72
00:06:57,530 --> 00:06:58,680
Move!

73
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:05,740
I heard they get all swollen

74
00:07:05,740 --> 00:07:07,800
and bruised if you don't use them.

75
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:10,030
Of course, maybe that's just what the lads say

76
00:07:10,030 --> 00:07:12,330
when they want me feeling sorry for them.

77
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:15,080
As if I'd feel sorry for them.

78
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:18,280
Are there no girl crows?

79
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:22,380
There are no women of the night's watch, no.

80
00:07:22,610 --> 00:07:24,460
So the lads just do it with each other?

81
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:25,520
No.

82
00:07:26,570 --> 00:07:28,540
- Never? - Never.

83
00:07:29,090 --> 00:07:30,440
We swore an oath.

84
00:07:31,870 --> 00:07:33,350
You have sheep at the wall?

85
00:07:36,210 --> 00:07:37,730
With your hands, then?

86
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:40,700
No wonder you're all so miserable.

87
00:07:41,820 --> 00:07:42,990
Would you please shut up?

88
00:07:42,990 --> 00:07:44,520
Would you please shut up?

89
00:07:45,970 --> 00:07:48,230
You think you're better than me, crow.

90
00:07:48,630 --> 00:07:51,020
- I'm a free woman-- - You're a free woman?

91
00:07:51,020 --> 00:07:53,260
I might be your prisoner, but I'm a free woman.

92
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:55,240
If you're my prisoner, you're not a free woman.

93
00:07:55,250 --> 00:07:57,270
That's what "Prisoner" means.

94
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:58,880
And you think you're free?

95
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:02,050
You swore some stupid oath

96
00:08:02,050 --> 00:08:03,660
and now you can never touch a girl.

97
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:05,790
It was my choice to say the words.

98
00:08:05,790 --> 00:08:08,010
- So you don't like girls? - Of course I like girls.

99
00:08:08,010 --> 00:08:09,580
But you chose never to touch them.

100
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:12,500
That's the price you pay if you want to be a man of the Night's Watch.

101
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:14,530
So instead of getting naked with a girl,

102
00:08:14,530 --> 00:08:16,070
you'd prefer to invade our lands--

103
00:08:16,070 --> 00:08:17,680
Invade your lands?

104
00:08:18,150 --> 00:08:19,990
Wildlings raid our lands all the time.

105
00:08:19,990 --> 00:08:22,710
Some of them tried to kill my little brother, a crippled boy!

106
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:24,700
They're not your lands!

107
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:26,870
We've been here the whole time.

108
00:08:26,870 --> 00:08:28,080
You lot came along and

109
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:30,730
just put up a big wall and said it was yours.

110
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:33,110
My father was Ned Stark.

111
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:35,030
I have the blood of the first men.

112
00:08:35,030 --> 00:08:38,000
My ancestors lived here, same as yours.

113
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,790
So why are you fighting us?

114
00:08:59,460 --> 00:09:00,620
Go on.

115
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:08,600
Now I want you to tell me what happened.

116
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:09,960
Come on, this way.

117
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:15,250
Come on, speak up. Speak up.

118
00:09:20,910 --> 00:09:22,090
Wolfsbane--

119
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:25,010
a rare substance.

120
00:09:26,110 --> 00:09:28,260
This is no common assassin.

121
00:09:28,450 --> 00:09:30,520
We hanged 20 men last night.

122
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:33,170
I don't care if you hanged 100.

123
00:09:33,700 --> 00:09:34,950
A man tried to kill me.

124
00:09:34,950 --> 00:09:36,950
I want his name and I want his head.

125
00:09:36,990 --> 00:09:41,220
We think it was an infiltrator from the Brotherhood without Banners.

126
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:44,250
Pretentious name for a band of outlaws.

127
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:48,830
We can't allow rebels behind our lines to harass us with impunity.

128
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:51,020
We look like fools and they look like heroes.

129
00:09:51,020 --> 00:09:52,670
That's how kings fall.

130
00:09:52,670 --> 00:09:55,050
I want them dead, every one.

131
00:09:55,050 --> 00:09:56,880
Killing them isn't the problem.

132
00:09:57,420 --> 00:09:58,760
It's finding them.

133
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,580
Have you gone soft, Clegane?

134
00:10:01,220 --> 00:10:03,510
I always thought you had a talent for violence.

135
00:10:03,530 --> 00:10:05,960
Burn the villages, burn the farms.

136
00:10:06,710 --> 00:10:09,580
Let them know what it means to choose the wrong side.

137
00:10:13,750 --> 00:10:14,750
Is that mutton?

138
00:10:15,530 --> 00:10:17,090
Yes, My Lord.

139
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:18,280
Don't like mutton.

140
00:10:19,970 --> 00:10:21,460
I'll bring something else.

141
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:22,790
Leave it.

142
00:10:24,980 --> 00:10:27,300
- Are you hungry? - No.

143
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:28,550
Of course you are.

144
00:10:29,750 --> 00:10:30,970
Eat.

145
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:34,150
I'll eat in the kitchen later.

146
00:10:34,210 --> 00:10:37,570
It's bad manners to refuse a lord's offer.

147
00:10:38,180 --> 00:10:39,350
Sit.

148
00:10:41,330 --> 00:10:42,500
Eat.

149
00:10:45,710 --> 00:10:47,410
You're small for your age.

150
00:10:49,170 --> 00:10:51,310
I suppose you've been underfed your whole life.

151
00:10:51,310 --> 00:10:52,640
I eat a lot.

152
00:10:53,090 --> 00:10:55,640
I just don't grow.

153
00:10:59,410 --> 00:11:01,490
This will be my last war,

154
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,810
win or lose.

155
00:11:06,310 --> 00:11:07,870
Have you ever lost before?

156
00:11:08,970 --> 00:11:11,950
Do you think I'd be in my position if I had lost a war?

157
00:11:18,590 --> 00:11:21,060
This is the one I'll be remembered for.

158
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:24,950
The "War of Five Kings" they're calling it.

159
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:29,790
My legacy will be determined in the coming months.

160
00:11:31,660 --> 00:11:33,390
Do you know what legacy means?

161
00:11:35,790 --> 00:11:38,220
It's what you pass down to your children

162
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:40,400
and your children's children.

163
00:11:41,830 --> 00:11:44,850
It's what remains of you when you're gone.

164
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:51,840
Harren the Black thought this castle would be his legacy.

165
00:11:53,590 --> 00:11:55,300
The greatest fortress ever built...

166
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:58,750
The tallest towers, the strongest walls.

167
00:11:59,610 --> 00:12:02,420
The great hall had 35 hearths.

168
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,400
35. Can you imagine?

169
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,810
Look at it now...

170
00:12:09,260 --> 00:12:10,740
a blasted ruin.

171
00:12:12,580 --> 00:12:13,790
Do you know what happened?

172
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:15,570
Dragons?

173
00:12:16,420 --> 00:12:19,960
Yes, dragons happened.

174
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:27,760
Harrenhal was built to withstand an attack from the land.

175
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:32,960
A million men could have marched on these walls

176
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:35,450
and a million men would have been repelled.

177
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:40,260
But an attack from the air with dragon fire... mm.

178
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:44,730
Harren and all his sons roasted alive within these walls.

179
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:48,300
Aegon Targaryen changed the rules.

180
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:52,140
That's why every child alive still knows his name

181
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:54,440
300 years after his death.

182
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:56,970
Aegon and his sisters.

183
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:02,340
It wasn't just Aegon riding his dragon.

184
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:04,930
It was Rhaenys and Visenya, too.

185
00:13:04,990 --> 00:13:06,300
Correct.

186
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:09,130
A student of history, are you?

187
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:11,290
Rhaenys rode Meraxes.

188
00:13:11,710 --> 00:13:13,560
Visenya rode Vhagar.

189
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:17,560
I'm sure I knew that when I was a boy.

190
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:20,480
Visenya Targaryen was a great warrior.

191
00:13:22,090 --> 00:13:25,190
She had a Valyrian steel sword she called Dark Sister.

192
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:29,570
She's a heroine of yours, I take it?

193
00:13:30,930 --> 00:13:34,210
Aren't most girls more interested in the pretty maidens from the songs?

194
00:13:34,210 --> 00:13:36,510
Jonquil with the flowers in her hair?

195
00:13:36,510 --> 00:13:38,880
Most girls are idiots.

196
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:42,610
You remind me of my daughter.

197
00:13:44,220 --> 00:13:45,440
Where did you learn all this stuff

198
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:49,370
about Visenya and her Valyrian steel sword?

199
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:52,070
From my father.

200
00:13:54,740 --> 00:13:56,740
He was a well-read stonemason.

201
00:13:58,390 --> 00:14:01,660
Can't say I've ever met a literate stonemason.

202
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:05,510
Have you met many stonemasons, My Lord?

203
00:14:07,710 --> 00:14:09,410
Careful now, girl.

204
00:14:09,670 --> 00:14:11,960
I enjoy you, but be careful.

205
00:14:12,270 --> 00:14:14,130
Take that back to the kitchen.

206
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:16,670
Eat what you want.

207
00:14:19,750 --> 00:14:20,980
And, girl.

208
00:14:23,540 --> 00:14:24,860
M'lord.

209
00:14:27,270 --> 00:14:29,880
Lowborn girls say "M'lord,"

210
00:14:29,890 --> 00:14:31,950
Not "My lord."

211
00:14:32,450 --> 00:14:34,020
If you're going to pose as a commoner,

212
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:35,660
you should do it properly.

213
00:14:37,900 --> 00:14:41,550
My mother served lady Dustin for many years, My Lord.

214
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:45,790
She taught me how to speak proper... properly.

215
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:49,620
You're too smart for your own good.

216
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:53,090
- Has anyone told you that? - Yes.

217
00:14:53,710 --> 00:14:54,930
Go on.

218
00:15:06,710 --> 00:15:08,410
I beg pardon, ser.

219
00:15:10,510 --> 00:15:12,400
I should have come to you after

220
00:15:12,470 --> 00:15:14,350
to thank you for saving me.

221
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:17,300
- You were so brave. - Brave?

222
00:15:17,870 --> 00:15:20,760
A dog doesn't need courage to chase off rats.

223
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:23,870
Does it give you joy to scare people?

224
00:15:24,070 --> 00:15:26,560
No. It gives me joy to kill people.

225
00:15:27,390 --> 00:15:28,560
Spare me. You can't tell me

226
00:15:28,570 --> 00:15:31,930
Lord Eddard Stark of Winterfell never killed a man.

227
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:35,100
It was his duty. He never liked it.

228
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:36,870
Is that what he told you?

229
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,590
He lied.

230
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:41,810
Killing is the sweetest thing there is.

231
00:15:42,710 --> 00:15:44,980
Why are you always so hateful?

232
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:47,880
You'll be glad of the hateful things I do someday when you're queen

233
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:52,760
and I'm all that stands between you and your beloved king.

234
00:16:01,740 --> 00:16:03,540
I've demanded a meeting of the thirteen.

235
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:05,120
One of them did this or knows who did.

236
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:06,830
You are one of the thirteen.

237
00:16:06,830 --> 00:16:08,880
If I wanted your dragons, I would have taken them.

238
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:12,280
- They mean nothing to me on their own. - Nothing?

239
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:14,930
They're more valuable than anything in the world.

240
00:16:14,930 --> 00:16:16,120
Shall we look inside my vault

241
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:17,620
and see what selling your dragons

242
00:16:17,620 --> 00:16:19,740
would buy me I cannot buy already?

243
00:16:20,050 --> 00:16:21,920
We will get them back.

244
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,610
There is no we,

245
00:16:23,610 --> 00:16:26,460
so why would you help me get them back?

246
00:16:26,460 --> 00:16:27,910
I took you under my protection

247
00:16:27,910 --> 00:16:30,070
in front of the rulers of my city.

248
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:33,020
A man is what others say he is and no more.

249
00:16:33,140 --> 00:16:35,970
If they say that Xaro Xhoan Daxos is a liar,

250
00:16:35,970 --> 00:16:37,990
my word is worth nothing.

251
00:16:38,430 --> 00:16:40,930
I cannot let this thing happen to you under my roof.

252
00:16:40,930 --> 00:16:43,270
But it did happen under your roof.

253
00:16:43,270 --> 00:16:46,830
Khaleesi, many times in my life I have been...

254
00:16:46,830 --> 00:16:48,650
I don't care where you've been.

255
00:17:11,570 --> 00:17:13,060
You think we're savages

256
00:17:13,060 --> 00:17:15,300
because we don't live in stone castles.

257
00:17:15,830 --> 00:17:19,020
We can't make steel as good as yours, it's true, but...

258
00:17:19,710 --> 00:17:21,020
we're free.

259
00:17:22,250 --> 00:17:23,110
If someone tried to tell us

260
00:17:23,110 --> 00:17:25,230
we couldn't lie down as man and woman,

261
00:17:25,230 --> 00:17:27,630
we'd shove a spear up his ass.

262
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:29,460
We don't go serving some shit king

263
00:17:29,460 --> 00:17:31,680
who's only king because his father was.

264
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:36,190
No. No, you serve Mance Rayder, the King-Beyond-the-Wall.

265
00:17:36,190 --> 00:17:38,850
We chose Mance Rayder to lead us.

266
00:17:39,410 --> 00:17:41,420
He was a crow, same as you,

267
00:17:41,950 --> 00:17:43,680
but he wanted to be free.

268
00:17:45,670 --> 00:17:47,140
You could be free, too.

269
00:17:48,370 --> 00:17:49,960
You don't need to live your whole life

270
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:51,960
taking commands from old men.

271
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:55,040
Wake up when you want to wake up.

272
00:17:55,630 --> 00:17:58,280
I could show you the streams to fish, the woods to hunt.

273
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:02,240
Build yourself a cabin and find a woman to lie with in the night.

274
00:18:04,370 --> 00:18:05,740
You're a pretty lad.

275
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:07,880
The girls would claw each other's eyes out

276
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:09,380
to get naked with you.

277
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:13,700
Walk.

278
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:18,030
I could teach you how to do it.

279
00:18:18,190 --> 00:18:19,720
I know how to do it.

280
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:25,950
You know nothing, Jon Snow.

281
00:18:55,210 --> 00:18:56,470
And what did she say?

282
00:18:56,890 --> 00:18:59,780
She admired your spirit, Your Grace.

283
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:01,340
And what then?

284
00:19:03,150 --> 00:19:04,520
She, uh...

285
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:07,480
If every man were held accountable

286
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,370
for the actions of every distant relative,

287
00:19:09,370 --> 00:19:12,620
Ser Alton, we'd all hang.

288
00:19:15,450 --> 00:19:18,130
She tore the paper in half, Your Grace.

289
00:19:19,250 --> 00:19:20,630
You've acted with honor.

290
00:19:20,630 --> 00:19:21,950
I thank you for it.

291
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:25,410
Lord Karstark, see that Ser Alton's pen is clean.

292
00:19:25,610 --> 00:19:27,090
And give him a hot supper.

293
00:19:27,090 --> 00:19:29,910
Ser Alton's pen is occupied, Your Grace.

294
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:32,430
The prisoners from the Yellow Fork.

295
00:19:32,790 --> 00:19:34,170
Too many prisoners.

296
00:19:35,110 --> 00:19:37,280
Is there room for Ser Alton?

297
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:39,780
Does he need to lie down?

298
00:19:42,980 --> 00:19:44,700
Have the men build him a new pen.

299
00:19:45,370 --> 00:19:47,470
Put him in with the Kingslayer for now.

300
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:49,720
Have your boy watch over them.

301
00:19:49,890 --> 00:19:51,020
Torrhen.

302
00:19:52,340 --> 00:19:53,520
That will be all.

303
00:20:00,790 --> 00:20:01,910
Your Grace.

304
00:20:02,380 --> 00:20:03,650
A minute of your time?

305
00:20:18,780 --> 00:20:20,670
I've been treating your wounded men.

306
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:22,720
And my enemies

307
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:25,140
as some of my bannermen are fond of mentioning.

308
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:26,780
They're not my enemies.

309
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:28,660
That's what I tell my bannermen.

310
00:20:29,060 --> 00:20:31,590
I've already run through the supplies I brought with me.

311
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:32,970
Some are easily replaced...

312
00:20:32,970 --> 00:20:36,490
egg yolks, turpentine, oil of roses.

313
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:38,350
But some are not.

314
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:41,200
I need silk for stitching.

315
00:20:42,790 --> 00:20:45,880
I need fennel root for those with fever, willow bark.

316
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,580
Mostly I need milk of the poppy.

317
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:50,690
You saw what it was like to amputate a foot without any.

318
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:55,010
I assume there will be more loss of limb before this war is over.

319
00:20:55,850 --> 00:20:58,490
- If you need help finding these... - I know where to find them.

320
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:02,180
I'm sorry, I shouldn't interrupt you.

321
00:21:03,530 --> 00:21:05,690
Continue, My Lady.

322
00:21:09,630 --> 00:21:13,110
- You're riding to the Crag to negotiate a surrender? - Yes.

323
00:21:13,370 --> 00:21:17,120
The Crag will have a Maester and he will have what I need.

324
00:21:17,390 --> 00:21:18,700
I expect he will.

325
00:21:18,910 --> 00:21:20,980
If I could write a list...

326
00:21:20,980 --> 00:21:22,550
Come with me to the Crag.

327
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:26,240
I don't think that will be...

328
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:28,420
Let the Maester show you his stores.

329
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:31,460
I want the wounded men to be treated well...

330
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:34,550
all the wounded men.

331
00:21:42,620 --> 00:21:45,070
Children, come inside, quick.

332
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:46,680
Hurry up!

333
00:21:49,370 --> 00:21:50,530
Can't find anything, Ser.

334
00:21:50,530 --> 00:21:53,230
- They've lost the scent. - Try again.

335
00:21:53,230 --> 00:21:54,760
We've circled this farmhouse twice.

336
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:56,300
There's no sign of them.

337
00:21:56,510 --> 00:21:59,690
We could start the search fresh in the morning, My Lord.

338
00:22:00,650 --> 00:22:02,410
I'm looking at spending the rest of my life

339
00:22:02,410 --> 00:22:05,560
being treated like a fool and a eunuch by my own people.

340
00:22:05,570 --> 00:22:07,620
Ask yourself, "Is there anything I wouldn't do

341
00:22:07,620 --> 00:22:09,240
to stop that from happening?"

342
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:11,020
The hounds will find the scent again.

343
00:22:11,020 --> 00:22:13,470
I'll beat them until they do.

344
00:22:13,470 --> 00:22:14,900
I'll whip every man here

345
00:22:14,900 --> 00:22:16,980
until I have both those boys in hand.

346
00:22:17,060 --> 00:22:20,090
And once I've got them, the pampered little shits...

347
00:22:22,030 --> 00:22:24,110
It's better to be cruel than weak.

348
00:22:24,450 --> 00:22:25,590
Prince Theon.

349
00:22:26,620 --> 00:22:28,190
- Where are they? - Who, M'lord?

350
00:22:28,190 --> 00:22:30,540
The Stark boys. Where are they?

351
00:22:30,690 --> 00:22:32,510
I don't know. I seen no one.

352
00:22:34,130 --> 00:22:35,340
Think harder.

353
00:22:36,170 --> 00:22:39,250
I swear, M'lord, I don't know.

354
00:22:39,910 --> 00:22:42,410
My Lord, over here.

355
00:22:45,730 --> 00:22:47,710
I think I've found what we're looking for.

356
00:22:58,180 --> 00:22:59,590
Send the old man home.

357
00:23:05,380 --> 00:23:06,760
Go back to Winterfell.

358
00:23:07,710 --> 00:23:08,910
Take him back.

359
00:23:11,710 --> 00:23:13,330
Theon, don't do this.

360
00:23:32,530 --> 00:23:33,830
You came back.

361
00:23:33,830 --> 00:23:35,400
As soon as I heard.

362
00:23:36,070 --> 00:23:37,370
Do you know anything?

363
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:41,560
- Irri is dead. - I know.

364
00:23:42,850 --> 00:23:44,860
- She was a good... - She's dead.

365
00:23:45,870 --> 00:23:46,820
She died alone.

366
00:23:46,830 --> 00:23:49,140
She died for me and I couldn't protect her.

367
00:23:50,640 --> 00:23:51,850
Doreah?

368
00:23:52,850 --> 00:23:54,450
We can't find her.

369
00:23:55,410 --> 00:23:56,880
She must be dead, too.

370
00:23:58,600 --> 00:24:00,470
I led my people out of the Red Waste

371
00:24:00,470 --> 00:24:02,290
and into the slaughterhouse.

372
00:24:02,490 --> 00:24:04,020
I should have been here.

373
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:07,000
You went to find me a ship.

374
00:24:07,580 --> 00:24:09,710
My place is by your side.

375
00:24:09,710 --> 00:24:12,150
I shouldn't have left you alone with these people.

376
00:24:12,740 --> 00:24:14,020
These people?

377
00:24:14,070 --> 00:24:15,940
They are not to be trusted.

378
00:24:16,030 --> 00:24:18,210
And who is to be trusted?

379
00:24:18,780 --> 00:24:20,780
Who are my people?

380
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:22,670
The Targaryens?

381
00:24:22,730 --> 00:24:24,510
I only knew one-- my brother,

382
00:24:24,510 --> 00:24:26,930
and he would have let 1,000 men rape me

383
00:24:26,930 --> 00:24:28,550
if it had got him the crown.

384
00:24:28,960 --> 00:24:30,410
The Dothraki?

385
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:32,050
Most of them turned on me

386
00:24:32,050 --> 00:24:34,440
the day that Khal Drogo fell from his horse.

387
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:36,210
Your people are in Westeros.

388
00:24:36,210 --> 00:24:38,680
The people in Westeros don't know I'm alive.

389
00:24:38,680 --> 00:24:40,940
- They will soon enough. - And then what?

390
00:24:40,940 --> 00:24:43,070
They'll pray for my return?

391
00:24:43,070 --> 00:24:46,040
They'll wave dragon banners and shout my name?

392
00:24:46,330 --> 00:24:48,670
That's what my brother believed and he was a fool.

393
00:24:48,910 --> 00:24:50,940
You are not your brother.

394
00:24:51,250 --> 00:24:53,410
Trust me, Khaleesi.

395
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:55,210
There it is...

396
00:24:56,040 --> 00:24:57,640
"Trust me."

397
00:24:58,360 --> 00:25:00,690
And it's you I should trust, Ser Jorah?

398
00:25:01,050 --> 00:25:02,360
Only you?

399
00:25:05,630 --> 00:25:08,430
I don't need trust any longer.

400
00:25:09,010 --> 00:25:11,490
I don't want it and I don't have room for it.

401
00:25:12,470 --> 00:25:13,910
You are too young to be so--

402
00:25:13,910 --> 00:25:15,720
And you are too familiar.

403
00:25:21,130 --> 00:25:22,520
Forgive me, Khaleesi.

404
00:25:25,110 --> 00:25:27,840
No one can survive in this world without help.

405
00:25:27,840 --> 00:25:29,220
No one.

406
00:25:29,470 --> 00:25:32,340
Let me help you, please.

407
00:25:32,910 --> 00:25:34,300
Tell me how.

408
00:25:36,510 --> 00:25:38,210
Find my dragons.

409
00:25:46,020 --> 00:25:48,300
How long till we get back to your crows?

410
00:25:50,420 --> 00:25:51,690
We're close.

411
00:25:52,210 --> 00:25:55,050
What, a day? A half-day?

412
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:01,240
You don't know, do you?

413
00:26:02,230 --> 00:26:05,000
- Do you even know where they are? - We're close.

414
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:08,880
What do you think they'll say when they hear about you and me?

415
00:26:08,880 --> 00:26:11,130
Nothing happened between you and me.

416
00:26:11,130 --> 00:26:14,450
"I swear it, old master king crow, ser,

417
00:26:14,450 --> 00:26:17,100
We were only close together for warmth.

418
00:26:17,330 --> 00:26:18,690
And then I felt it,

419
00:26:18,690 --> 00:26:21,470
right up against me backside like a club.

420
00:26:21,470 --> 00:26:24,210
I can show you the bruise on me tailbone.

421
00:26:24,210 --> 00:26:27,480
And before I knew what was where, his... his...

422
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:30,520
well, it was all out in the open, all angry as you like.

423
00:26:30,520 --> 00:26:34,480
And I didn't want to want it, but, oh, I did!

424
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:37,700
And he spread me legs and... ruined.

425
00:26:37,700 --> 00:26:39,080
The shame of it.

426
00:26:39,140 --> 00:26:41,430
Now I can never marry a perfumed lord.

427
00:26:41,430 --> 00:26:45,360
- What will my poor savage father say?" - Turn back around.

428
00:26:45,370 --> 00:26:47,210
"And I thought that we were done, but he said,

429
00:26:47,210 --> 00:26:48,760
'turn back around.'"

430
00:26:50,710 --> 00:26:52,490
I'll tell you what, Jon Snow,

431
00:26:52,930 --> 00:26:54,950
since it's going to be your word against mine,

432
00:26:54,950 --> 00:26:58,250
and since you can't talk about it without blushing,

433
00:26:59,150 --> 00:27:01,680
we may as well just.

434
00:27:02,950 --> 00:27:04,670
What, right here in the muck?

435
00:27:05,280 --> 00:27:06,840
I'll keep you warm enough.

436
00:27:09,230 --> 00:27:10,920
Are you that afraid of it?

437
00:27:11,940 --> 00:27:12,890
That's enough.

438
00:27:12,890 --> 00:27:14,390
Oh, it's nice

439
00:27:15,310 --> 00:27:18,430
and wet and warm.

440
00:27:18,430 --> 00:27:19,610
Enough!

441
00:27:21,390 --> 00:27:23,130
It don't have teeth.

442
00:27:31,100 --> 00:27:32,280
All right!

443
00:27:33,580 --> 00:27:34,800
All right.

444
00:27:36,650 --> 00:27:38,160
Gods, you're dull.

445
00:28:14,390 --> 00:28:16,670
Should have took me while you had the chance.

446
00:28:28,510 --> 00:28:30,170
No, no!

447
00:28:48,900 --> 00:28:51,000
No. Oh, no.

448
00:29:07,730 --> 00:29:09,910
It's all right. Give me that.

449
00:29:09,910 --> 00:29:13,950
If the queen sees I can have Joffrey's children now...

450
00:29:14,390 --> 00:29:15,630
Help me flip it over.

451
00:29:32,710 --> 00:29:33,710
Where are you going?

452
00:29:33,710 --> 00:29:35,210
To tell her grace.

453
00:29:37,300 --> 00:29:39,410
You'll say nothing to anyone.

454
00:29:39,410 --> 00:29:40,920
Do you understand?

455
00:30:02,650 --> 00:30:04,580
Your mother might have prepared you.

456
00:30:05,180 --> 00:30:07,010
You flowered, my dear. No more.

457
00:30:07,730 --> 00:30:10,920
My mother told me, but I thought it would be different.

458
00:30:10,920 --> 00:30:12,200
In what way?

459
00:30:12,970 --> 00:30:15,290
I thought it would be less--

460
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:17,330
less messy.

461
00:30:18,980 --> 00:30:20,640
Wait until you bear the child.

462
00:30:23,500 --> 00:30:26,270
You're a woman now. Do you have any idea what that means?

463
00:30:27,110 --> 00:30:29,050
I'm fit to bear children for the king?

464
00:30:30,020 --> 00:30:32,080
A prospect that once delighted you...

465
00:30:32,310 --> 00:30:34,980
bringing little princes and princesses into the world,

466
00:30:36,120 --> 00:30:38,430
the greatest honor for a queen.

467
00:30:43,250 --> 00:30:44,950
Joffrey has always been difficult.

468
00:30:46,370 --> 00:30:48,410
Even his birth, I labored a day and a half

469
00:30:48,410 --> 00:30:49,830
to bring him into this world.

470
00:30:50,340 --> 00:30:52,200
You cannot imagine the pain.

471
00:30:53,030 --> 00:30:54,810
I screamed so loudly,

472
00:30:54,810 --> 00:30:56,680
I'm sure Robert would hear me in the kingswood.

473
00:30:57,160 --> 00:30:58,820
His grace was not with you?

474
00:30:59,030 --> 00:31:00,240
Robert was hunting.

475
00:31:01,170 --> 00:31:02,500
That was his custom.

476
00:31:05,590 --> 00:31:07,340
Whenever my time was near,

477
00:31:08,080 --> 00:31:11,350
my royal husband would flee to the trees

478
00:31:11,350 --> 00:31:14,850
with his huntsmen and his hounds.

479
00:31:15,860 --> 00:31:17,100
And when he returned, he would present me

480
00:31:17,100 --> 00:31:19,920
with some pelts or a stag's head,

481
00:31:20,680 --> 00:31:22,420
and I would present him with a baby.

482
00:31:24,640 --> 00:31:26,230
Not that I wanted him there, mind you.

483
00:31:26,950 --> 00:31:29,710
I had grand maester Pycelle, an army of midwives,

484
00:31:29,710 --> 00:31:31,210
and I had my brother.

485
00:31:32,060 --> 00:31:34,700
When they told Jaime he wasn't allowed in the birthing room,

486
00:31:35,450 --> 00:31:40,230
He smiled and asked which one of them proposed to keep him out.

487
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:46,060
Joffrey will show you no such devotion.

488
00:31:48,910 --> 00:31:50,400
You may never love the king,

489
00:31:51,430 --> 00:31:52,890
but you will love his children.

490
00:31:53,810 --> 00:31:55,800
I love his grace with all my heart.

491
00:31:57,420 --> 00:31:59,120
That's so very touching to hear.

492
00:32:04,170 --> 00:32:06,040
Permit me to share some womanly wisdom

493
00:32:06,040 --> 00:32:07,820
with you on this very special day.

494
00:32:09,350 --> 00:32:11,640
The more people you love, the weaker you are.

495
00:32:13,410 --> 00:32:15,930
You'll do things for them that you know you shouldn't do.

496
00:32:16,890 --> 00:32:20,530
You'll act the fool to make them happy, to keep them safe.

497
00:32:23,190 --> 00:32:25,100
Love no one but your children.

498
00:32:25,740 --> 00:32:27,760
On that front, a mother has no choice.

499
00:32:30,210 --> 00:32:33,360
But... shouldn't I love Joffrey, Your Grace?

500
00:32:36,420 --> 00:32:37,460
You can try,

501
00:32:39,530 --> 00:32:40,610
little dove.

502
00:32:57,190 --> 00:32:58,920
Who did you say your mother was again?

503
00:33:00,210 --> 00:33:01,580
Cinda Lannister.

504
00:33:02,180 --> 00:33:03,290
Is she the fat one?

505
00:33:04,550 --> 00:33:06,400
Well, perhaps she's gotten a little larger than she...

506
00:33:06,400 --> 00:33:09,820
No, no. There's only one fat Lannister.

507
00:33:10,230 --> 00:33:12,090
If she was your mother, you'd know it.

508
00:33:14,570 --> 00:33:17,190
I squired for you once, you know?

509
00:33:19,030 --> 00:33:19,680
When?

510
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:22,970
The tournament the day of Willem Frey's wedding.

511
00:33:24,140 --> 00:33:26,290
I went to Willem Frey's wedding?

512
00:33:26,850 --> 00:33:27,710
You did.

513
00:33:28,760 --> 00:33:31,580
Your squire had gotten so drunk the night before that he--

514
00:33:31,770 --> 00:33:33,190
He threw up on his horse

515
00:33:33,190 --> 00:33:34,890
on the way to the tourney grounds.

516
00:33:34,890 --> 00:33:36,380
What was his name?

517
00:33:36,930 --> 00:33:37,630
Bryan.

518
00:33:38,940 --> 00:33:39,970
Poor lad.

519
00:33:40,850 --> 00:33:43,070
That was my brother's doing, I seem to recall.

520
00:33:46,040 --> 00:33:47,180
I remember you.

521
00:33:48,290 --> 00:33:50,760
You had never squired for anyone before.

522
00:33:50,930 --> 00:33:52,920
That's right. I ran up and volunteered.

523
00:33:52,920 --> 00:33:54,490
"Let me, My Lord. Let me."

524
00:33:56,610 --> 00:33:58,160
My father was furious,

525
00:33:59,270 --> 00:34:03,360
afraid I'd embarrass our family in front of the family.

526
00:34:05,090 --> 00:34:06,230
You didn't, though.

527
00:34:07,170 --> 00:34:08,610
You really remember?

528
00:34:09,240 --> 00:34:11,820
You knew when you were needed and when to go away.

529
00:34:11,820 --> 00:34:13,080
It's a rare talent.

530
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:16,950
Most of my squires, they mean well,

531
00:34:17,230 --> 00:34:20,730
but young men with big jobs, they tend to overdo them.

532
00:34:21,190 --> 00:34:22,950
Well, when I think back to that day--

533
00:34:32,390 --> 00:34:33,700
You were saying?

534
00:34:34,420 --> 00:34:34,960
I...

535
00:34:36,900 --> 00:34:39,590
never mind. It's embarrassing.

536
00:34:39,590 --> 00:34:42,580
More embarrassing than being chained to a post

537
00:34:42,580 --> 00:34:44,340
covered in your own shit?

538
00:34:45,590 --> 00:34:48,190
I remember everything about that day--

539
00:34:48,190 --> 00:34:49,870
your helmet, your horse,

540
00:34:50,520 --> 00:34:52,760
the rake lines in the dirt along the list.

541
00:34:53,430 --> 00:34:54,640
Where the sun was in the sky

542
00:34:54,640 --> 00:34:56,780
when you knocked Balon Swann from his horse,

543
00:34:57,200 --> 00:35:00,260
and the dent in your shield when you handed it back to me.

544
00:35:02,310 --> 00:35:04,350
I'll remember it all until I die.

545
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:08,640
That was the best day of my life.

546
00:35:11,690 --> 00:35:15,420
And I remember being on the field after it was over.

547
00:35:15,900 --> 00:35:17,040
All the competitors were done.

548
00:35:17,040 --> 00:35:18,550
I was the last one out there.

549
00:35:21,290 --> 00:35:22,500
And I couldn't leave.

550
00:35:24,230 --> 00:35:26,260
I couldn't bring myself to go and sit with my family

551
00:35:26,260 --> 00:35:28,130
at a table so far on the edge of the feast

552
00:35:28,130 --> 00:35:29,720
you could barely even see the bride.

553
00:35:30,690 --> 00:35:33,260
And I couldn't bear to tell them what it had been like squiring for you

554
00:35:34,150 --> 00:35:36,000
when I knew that they could never have the faintest idea

555
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:37,510
what I was talking about.

556
00:35:39,350 --> 00:35:40,820
I understand completely.

557
00:35:41,280 --> 00:35:42,310
How could you?

558
00:35:44,650 --> 00:35:47,180
Sorry, I... I didn't mean to doubt you.

559
00:35:47,180 --> 00:35:49,600
- It's just that I...- - I was 16 once.

560
00:35:50,790 --> 00:35:53,950
I also had to replace someone's squire on short notice.

561
00:35:54,620 --> 00:35:55,750
Which knight was it?

562
00:35:56,520 --> 00:35:57,860
Barristan Selmy.

563
00:36:00,330 --> 00:36:03,150
The fight against the kingswood outlaws before your time.

564
00:36:05,070 --> 00:36:06,230
What was he like?

565
00:36:09,180 --> 00:36:10,460
He was

566
00:36:12,300 --> 00:36:13,650
a painter,

567
00:36:15,520 --> 00:36:18,070
a painter who only used red.

568
00:36:21,280 --> 00:36:26,640
I couldn't imagine being able to fight like that, not back then.

569
00:36:27,570 --> 00:36:28,720
And to help him do that,

570
00:36:28,720 --> 00:36:31,810
to be a part of something that perfect...

571
00:36:34,110 --> 00:36:36,610
I don't need to explain how that felt, not to you.

572
00:36:37,850 --> 00:36:39,330
It's hard to put into words.

573
00:36:39,330 --> 00:36:42,860
It's like stepping into a dream

574
00:36:42,860 --> 00:36:45,540
you've been dreaming for as long as you can remember

575
00:36:45,540 --> 00:36:47,730
and finding out that the dream

576
00:36:47,730 --> 00:36:49,780
is more real than your life.

577
00:36:53,100 --> 00:36:54,940
Leaving that battlefield was

578
00:36:56,120 --> 00:36:58,270
like being dragged off to prison.

579
00:36:59,100 --> 00:37:01,010
- Did you squire for him again? - No.

580
00:37:02,840 --> 00:37:04,510
I didn't have your gift.

581
00:37:05,980 --> 00:37:08,250
He couldn't take a step without stepping on me.

582
00:37:08,940 --> 00:37:11,020
I was awful, a complete liability...

583
00:37:12,400 --> 00:37:15,900
Until one of the outlaws

584
00:37:15,900 --> 00:37:19,250
decided to take on a 16-year-old squire.

585
00:37:25,190 --> 00:37:27,020
It's a good thing I am who I am.

586
00:37:29,010 --> 00:37:31,010
I'd have been useless at anything else.

587
00:37:36,110 --> 00:37:39,060
I'm not well-suited for imprisonment.

588
00:37:39,060 --> 00:37:40,410
Shocking, I know.

589
00:37:41,050 --> 00:37:42,250
Some men are.

590
00:37:43,020 --> 00:37:44,640
Ned Stark...

591
00:37:45,370 --> 00:37:48,930
I imagine he made an excellent prisoner right up until the end.

592
00:37:49,700 --> 00:37:50,610
But me, though...

593
00:37:52,030 --> 00:37:55,530
my life has left me uniquely unfit for constraint.

594
00:37:58,100 --> 00:37:59,360
Have you thought about...?

595
00:38:00,160 --> 00:38:01,000
Of course.

596
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:01,980
Every day.

597
00:38:02,770 --> 00:38:03,370
And?

598
00:38:05,610 --> 00:38:09,680
Good prisoners breed good jailers, apparently.

599
00:38:10,150 --> 00:38:11,530
The Starks are very careful.

600
00:38:13,510 --> 00:38:15,940
But there is a way, I think.

601
00:38:17,710 --> 00:38:19,760
It wasn't possible until now.

602
00:38:21,010 --> 00:38:21,930
What is it?

603
00:38:27,710 --> 00:38:30,530
- It's actually quite simple. - Well, let me help you.

604
00:38:30,530 --> 00:38:33,200
You'll only have to do one thing.

605
00:38:33,340 --> 00:38:34,530
Tell me.

606
00:38:37,790 --> 00:38:39,410
You'll have to die.

607
00:39:33,340 --> 00:39:34,720
Jorah the Andal.

608
00:39:36,170 --> 00:39:38,790
This man must sail past old Valyria.

609
00:39:39,290 --> 00:39:43,030
All who travel too close to the doom must have protection.

610
00:39:43,030 --> 00:39:45,150
I didn't come here for lessons.

611
00:39:45,150 --> 00:39:47,580
No, you came for the dragons.

612
00:39:47,960 --> 00:39:48,850
You have them?

613
00:39:50,860 --> 00:39:52,010
Where are they?

614
00:39:52,900 --> 00:39:54,240
Draw your sword.

615
00:39:55,720 --> 00:39:58,480
See what your steel is worth.

616
00:40:00,920 --> 00:40:03,440
You want to please the Mother of Dragons.

617
00:40:10,350 --> 00:40:11,580
You love her.

618
00:40:15,650 --> 00:40:17,110
Where are the dragons?

619
00:40:19,060 --> 00:40:21,210
Will you betray her again, Jorah the Andal?

620
00:40:26,550 --> 00:40:28,440
Will you betray her again?

621
00:40:31,340 --> 00:40:32,580
Never.

622
00:40:38,920 --> 00:40:40,740
The thief you seek

623
00:40:41,610 --> 00:40:43,160
is with her now.

624
00:40:48,930 --> 00:40:50,700
I did not leave the comfort of my home

625
00:40:50,700 --> 00:40:52,420
to come to yours and be called a thief.

626
00:40:52,420 --> 00:40:54,350
No one is calling you a thief.

627
00:40:54,350 --> 00:40:56,040
Who is she to accuse us?

628
00:40:56,040 --> 00:40:58,170
Please, they're my children.

629
00:40:58,170 --> 00:41:00,440
- I'm begging you. - Begging us?

630
00:41:00,600 --> 00:41:03,340
It wasn't very long ago you were threatening us.

631
00:41:03,340 --> 00:41:05,680
Without me, the dragons will die.

632
00:41:05,680 --> 00:41:07,450
It will be for the best.

633
00:41:07,910 --> 00:41:12,460
Your dragons will bring the world nothing but death and misery, my dear.

634
00:41:13,110 --> 00:41:15,380
If I knew where they were, I would not tell you.

635
00:41:15,470 --> 00:41:17,130
You are cruel, my friend.

636
00:41:18,090 --> 00:41:19,950
The Mother of Dragons is in the right.

637
00:41:20,750 --> 00:41:23,150
She must be reunited with her babies.

638
00:41:24,220 --> 00:41:26,450
I will help you, Khaleesi.

639
00:41:26,660 --> 00:41:27,470
How?

640
00:41:28,290 --> 00:41:30,640
I will take you to the House of the Undying

641
00:41:31,350 --> 00:41:32,690
where I have put them.

642
00:41:34,150 --> 00:41:36,010
You have my dragons?

643
00:41:36,190 --> 00:41:38,110
When I learned you were coming to our city,

644
00:41:38,630 --> 00:41:41,320
I made an arrangement with the king of Qarth.

645
00:41:43,220 --> 00:41:44,560
He procured them for me.

646
00:41:45,060 --> 00:41:48,090
- But there is no king of Qarth. - There is now.

647
00:41:48,090 --> 00:41:49,950
That was the other half of the arrangement.

648
00:41:53,130 --> 00:41:55,650
You would keep your gates and your minds closed

649
00:41:55,650 --> 00:41:57,920
to everything outside your walls,

650
00:41:58,440 --> 00:42:01,380
but Qarth cannot remain the greatest city that ever was

651
00:42:01,380 --> 00:42:03,180
if it refuses to change.

652
00:42:03,180 --> 00:42:05,600
I will open Qarth to the world

653
00:42:05,790 --> 00:42:08,270
as I have forced it to open itself to me.

654
00:42:09,650 --> 00:42:12,320
Your ambition is an inspiration.

655
00:42:13,040 --> 00:42:16,060
But like all upstarts, you overreach.

656
00:42:16,660 --> 00:42:19,150
Three dragons the size of cats

657
00:42:19,150 --> 00:42:21,170
and an alliance with a charlatan

658
00:42:21,170 --> 00:42:23,120
do not make you a king.

659
00:42:23,520 --> 00:42:25,060
An upstart and a charlatan?

660
00:42:26,200 --> 00:42:27,990
Empires have been built by less.

661
00:42:29,040 --> 00:42:32,280
Those on the margins often come to control the center,

662
00:42:32,720 --> 00:42:34,810
and those in the center make room for them,

663
00:42:35,060 --> 00:42:36,760
willingly or otherwise.

664
00:42:41,320 --> 00:42:43,840
The Mother of Dragons will be with her babies.

665
00:42:45,900 --> 00:42:47,260
She will give them her love

666
00:42:47,260 --> 00:42:49,500
and they will thrive by her side...

667
00:42:53,470 --> 00:42:54,610
forever.

668
00:43:14,540 --> 00:43:16,530
A mother should be with her children.

669
00:43:20,060 --> 00:43:22,530
Where will you run to, Daenerys Stormborn?

670
00:43:23,330 --> 00:43:25,950
Your dragons wait for you in the House of the Undying.

671
00:43:26,670 --> 00:43:27,950
Come see them.

672
00:43:37,970 --> 00:43:39,510
- Lady Stark! - No farther.

673
00:43:39,890 --> 00:43:41,450
Keep your hands off me, woman.

674
00:43:41,450 --> 00:43:45,000
Don't enter without an invitation, man.

675
00:43:46,360 --> 00:43:48,270
Forgive me. Lady Stark.

676
00:43:48,810 --> 00:43:51,330
- What is it? - They caught the Kingslayer.

677
00:43:57,370 --> 00:43:59,850
- Kill the fucking Kingslayer! - Hang him!

678
00:44:03,880 --> 00:44:05,030
You'll die today.

679
00:44:05,660 --> 00:44:07,500
Justice for the Karstark.

680
00:44:20,320 --> 00:44:21,210
Gut him!

681
00:44:35,160 --> 00:44:37,360
Get back! I want his head!

682
00:44:38,710 --> 00:44:43,460
Any man who stands between a father and his vengeance asks for death.

683
00:44:43,660 --> 00:44:44,860
Lord Karstark,

684
00:44:46,330 --> 00:44:48,170
this man is our prisoner.

685
00:44:49,040 --> 00:44:50,820
This monster killed my son.

686
00:44:50,820 --> 00:44:52,340
And crippled mine.

687
00:44:52,850 --> 00:44:54,520
He will answer for his crimes,

688
00:44:54,520 --> 00:44:56,710
I promise you, but not here.

689
00:44:56,710 --> 00:44:59,040
I will have his head. And if you try and stop me...

690
00:44:59,040 --> 00:45:00,500
You will strike me down?

691
00:45:01,330 --> 00:45:03,330
Have you forgotten me, ser?

692
00:45:03,950 --> 00:45:06,360
I am the widow of your liege lord Eddark Stark.

693
00:45:06,360 --> 00:45:07,890
I am the mother of your king!

694
00:45:07,890 --> 00:45:10,130
- And where is our king now? - You know very well.

695
00:45:10,500 --> 00:45:12,540
He has gone to the Crag to accept the surrender.

696
00:45:12,540 --> 00:45:16,190
Aye, gone to the Crag, but not to negotiate.

697
00:45:16,190 --> 00:45:18,170
He brought that foreign bitch with him.

698
00:45:18,170 --> 00:45:21,110
- How dare you? - Threatening my lady is an act of treason.

699
00:45:21,110 --> 00:45:21,970
Treason?

700
00:45:21,970 --> 00:45:24,310
How can it be treason to kill Lannisters?

701
00:45:24,310 --> 00:45:26,150
I understand your grief, My Lord--

702
00:45:26,150 --> 00:45:28,260
Better than most I understand it...

703
00:45:28,810 --> 00:45:31,420
But in the name of my son, the King in the North,

704
00:45:31,830 --> 00:45:33,540
stand down.

705
00:45:35,300 --> 00:45:37,140
When your son returns,

706
00:45:37,610 --> 00:45:39,490
I will demand this murderer's head.

707
00:45:39,490 --> 00:45:41,940
Wise men do not make demands of kings.

708
00:45:41,940 --> 00:45:44,480
Fathers who love their sons do.

709
00:45:45,010 --> 00:45:46,790
I will have his head.

710
00:45:49,420 --> 00:45:52,100
Thank you for fighting on my behalf, Lady Stark.

711
00:45:52,640 --> 00:45:54,460
I would have come to your defense, but...

712
00:45:54,910 --> 00:45:56,410
Take him to the stockades.

713
00:45:57,220 --> 00:45:59,320
Bind him with every chain you can find!

714
00:45:59,320 --> 00:46:01,390
You've become a real she-wolf in your later years.

715
00:46:01,840 --> 00:46:03,320
There's not much fish left in you.

716
00:46:03,420 --> 00:46:04,730
And gag him!

717
00:46:10,160 --> 00:46:12,120
Since when do you light your own candles?

718
00:46:12,880 --> 00:46:14,740
Since I decided that I can't stand to look

719
00:46:14,740 --> 00:46:17,840
at any of my handmaidens for another instant.

720
00:46:20,010 --> 00:46:22,830
How many times can you read one raven scroll?

721
00:46:23,380 --> 00:46:26,710
Stannis Baratheon's fleet has been spotted sailing north

722
00:46:26,710 --> 00:46:29,390
past Tarth... 200 ships.

723
00:46:29,390 --> 00:46:33,090
- More than we have. - Yes, that's more than we have.

724
00:46:34,000 --> 00:46:35,890
He'll be at our gates within five days,

725
00:46:35,890 --> 00:46:37,330
four if he has the wind.

726
00:46:37,520 --> 00:46:39,300
We have strong, high walls.

727
00:46:40,600 --> 00:46:42,850
We'll rain fire down on them from above.

728
00:46:43,940 --> 00:46:45,600
"Rain fire on them from above."

729
00:46:45,600 --> 00:46:47,600
You're quoting father, aren't you?

730
00:46:47,600 --> 00:46:48,560
Why not?

731
00:46:49,130 --> 00:46:51,010
He has a good mind for strategy, doesn't he?

732
00:46:52,220 --> 00:46:53,690
We call it tactics, not strategy.

733
00:46:53,690 --> 00:46:55,640
But, yes, he does have a good mind for it.

734
00:46:56,050 --> 00:46:57,690
The best mind, some would say.

735
00:46:57,690 --> 00:46:59,470
Sadly, he's not here.

736
00:47:00,840 --> 00:47:02,690
It's just you, me, and Joffrey,

737
00:47:03,470 --> 00:47:05,180
the Lord of the Seven kingdoms

738
00:47:05,180 --> 00:47:06,890
and Protector of the Realm.

739
00:47:08,900 --> 00:47:10,490
I'm sure you'll make a point eventually.

740
00:47:10,490 --> 00:47:12,960
He needs to start acting like a king.

741
00:47:13,920 --> 00:47:16,540
This war you started is coming to our doorstep.

742
00:47:17,280 --> 00:47:19,440
And if the entire city wants Joffrey dead--

743
00:47:19,440 --> 00:47:21,740
I'm not the one giving the boy whores to abuse.

744
00:47:22,730 --> 00:47:24,150
I thought the girls might help him.

745
00:47:24,150 --> 00:47:25,580
- Did you? - I was wrong.

746
00:47:29,110 --> 00:47:30,490
If we can't control him...

747
00:47:31,710 --> 00:47:32,960
Do you think I haven't tried?

748
00:47:35,730 --> 00:47:37,360
He doesn't listen to me.

749
00:47:40,390 --> 00:47:42,730
It's hard to put a leash on a dog

750
00:47:43,440 --> 00:47:45,820
once you've put a crown on its head.

751
00:47:49,420 --> 00:47:51,480
I always hoped he'd be like Jaime.

752
00:47:54,180 --> 00:47:55,450
He looks like him...

753
00:47:59,580 --> 00:48:00,960
in a certain light.

754
00:48:04,910 --> 00:48:06,590
The boy is more Robert than Jaime.

755
00:48:07,170 --> 00:48:09,960
Robert was a drunken fool, but he didn't enjoy cruelty.

756
00:48:13,000 --> 00:48:14,380
Sometimes I wonder...

757
00:48:15,690 --> 00:48:16,550
What?

758
00:48:18,380 --> 00:48:19,660
If this is the price

759
00:48:21,530 --> 00:48:25,050
for what we've done, for our sins.

760
00:48:26,010 --> 00:48:27,020
Sins?

761
00:48:28,640 --> 00:48:29,570
The Targaryens...

762
00:48:29,570 --> 00:48:32,250
Wed brother and sister for hundreds of years, I know.

763
00:48:34,950 --> 00:48:38,140
That's what Jaime and I would say to each other in our moments of doubt.

764
00:48:38,610 --> 00:48:40,030
It's what I told Ned Stark

765
00:48:40,030 --> 00:48:42,210
when he was stupid enough to confront me.

766
00:48:44,580 --> 00:48:46,790
Half the Targaryens went mad, didn't they?

767
00:48:47,500 --> 00:48:48,780
What's the saying?

768
00:48:49,090 --> 00:48:52,080
Every time a Targaryen is born, the gods flip a coin.

769
00:48:53,660 --> 00:48:55,350
You've beaten the odds.

770
00:48:55,920 --> 00:48:59,800
Tommen and Myrcella are good, decent children, both of them.

771
00:49:28,620 --> 00:49:31,210
- Why wait? - We're sworn to the king.

772
00:49:31,210 --> 00:49:33,600
- There's not a king. - That's treason.

773
00:49:33,600 --> 00:49:35,790
So is saving Lannisters, yeah?

774
00:49:35,790 --> 00:49:38,810
- Back off, you. - No, I won't.

775
00:49:38,810 --> 00:49:40,910
Your son returns at dawn, My Lady?

776
00:49:41,590 --> 00:49:42,620
So they say.

777
00:49:42,870 --> 00:49:44,670
The Kingslayer won't last the night.

778
00:49:46,330 --> 00:49:48,480
The more they drink, the angrier they'll get.

779
00:49:49,320 --> 00:49:51,600
And when the Karstarks draw their swords...

780
00:49:52,490 --> 00:49:54,770
who wants to die defending a Lannister?

781
00:49:56,270 --> 00:49:56,980
Come.

782
00:50:13,970 --> 00:50:15,530
I need to be alone with him.

783
00:50:15,920 --> 00:50:19,210
- My lady, our orders... - Your orders, which I just gave you,

784
00:50:19,790 --> 00:50:21,550
are to leave me alone with him.

785
00:50:27,320 --> 00:50:29,180
Come to say goodbye, Lady Stark?

786
00:50:30,410 --> 00:50:32,810
I believe it's my last night in this world.

787
00:50:34,450 --> 00:50:35,620
Is that a woman?

788
00:50:36,160 --> 00:50:37,530
Do you hear them out there?

789
00:50:38,710 --> 00:50:40,420
They want your head.

790
00:50:42,130 --> 00:50:44,820
Well, old Lord Karstark doesn't seem to like me.

791
00:50:44,820 --> 00:50:48,080
You strangled his son with your chains.

792
00:50:48,080 --> 00:50:49,520
Oh, oh.

793
00:50:50,440 --> 00:50:52,040
Was he the one on guard duty?

794
00:50:54,590 --> 00:50:55,760
He was in my way.

795
00:50:56,420 --> 00:50:57,970
Any knight would have done the same.

796
00:50:57,970 --> 00:50:59,520
You are no knight.

797
00:51:00,370 --> 00:51:02,570
You have forsaken every vow you ever took.

798
00:51:02,570 --> 00:51:04,090
So many vows.

799
00:51:04,680 --> 00:51:06,490
They make you swear and swear.

800
00:51:07,540 --> 00:51:09,470
Defend the king, obey the king,

801
00:51:09,470 --> 00:51:10,940
obey your father,

802
00:51:11,110 --> 00:51:13,400
protect the innocent, defend the weak.

803
00:51:14,190 --> 00:51:16,890
But what if your father despises the king?

804
00:51:18,210 --> 00:51:21,340
What if the king massacres the innocent?

805
00:51:21,950 --> 00:51:23,180
It's too much.

806
00:51:24,090 --> 00:51:27,410
No matter what you do, you're forsaking one vow or another.

807
00:51:27,950 --> 00:51:30,380
Where did you find this beast?

808
00:51:31,720 --> 00:51:34,670
She is a truer knight than you will ever be,

809
00:51:35,640 --> 00:51:36,770
Kingslayer.

810
00:51:36,770 --> 00:51:38,250
Kingslayer.

811
00:51:39,800 --> 00:51:41,490
What a king he was.

812
00:51:42,020 --> 00:51:45,340
Here's to Aerys Targaryen, the second of his name,

813
00:51:45,340 --> 00:51:48,550
Lord of the Seven Kingdoms, Protector of the Realm,

814
00:51:49,020 --> 00:51:51,850
and to the sword I shoved in his back.

815
00:51:54,040 --> 00:51:55,770
You are a man without honor.

816
00:51:58,560 --> 00:51:59,520
Do you know

817
00:52:00,650 --> 00:52:03,120
I've never been with any woman but Cersei?

818
00:52:03,850 --> 00:52:05,500
So in my own way,

819
00:52:06,490 --> 00:52:11,490
I have more honor than poor old dead Ned.

820
00:52:13,680 --> 00:52:15,780
What was the name of that bastard he fathered?

821
00:52:15,780 --> 00:52:17,700
- Brienne. - No, that wasn't it.

822
00:52:19,620 --> 00:52:22,930
Snow, a bastard from the north.

823
00:52:24,550 --> 00:52:26,700
Now, when... when good old Ned

824
00:52:26,700 --> 00:52:28,990
came home with some whore's baby,

825
00:52:29,870 --> 00:52:31,820
did you pretend to love it?

826
00:52:33,250 --> 00:52:36,740
No. You're not very good at pretending.

827
00:52:37,210 --> 00:52:38,900
You're an honest woman.

828
00:52:40,030 --> 00:52:42,280
You hated that boy, didn't you?

829
00:52:43,340 --> 00:52:44,770
How could you not hate him?

830
00:52:45,510 --> 00:52:48,000
The walking, talking reminder

831
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:51,650
that the honorable Lord Eddark Stark

832
00:52:51,650 --> 00:52:53,550
fucked another woman.

833
00:52:56,890 --> 00:52:57,850
Your sword.

834
00:53:04,050 --> 00:53:05,710
I told you what would happen.

835
00:53:07,310 --> 00:53:08,400
All of you...

836
00:53:10,480 --> 00:53:13,760
I told you what would happen if you served me loyally...

837
00:53:15,110 --> 00:53:17,300
and what would happen if you did not.

838
00:53:17,480 --> 00:53:18,530
What are you doing?

839
00:53:18,910 --> 00:53:21,310
- What have you done? - If there's any who still question

840
00:53:21,310 --> 00:53:24,070
whether your new lord means what he says...

841
00:53:27,180 --> 00:53:29,420
Here is the answer to your question.

842
00:53:29,660 --> 00:53:30,960
No!

